  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Asian Elephant Conservation Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Recipient will provide staff training and related capacity development for the staff in project protected areas, introduce Management Information System (MIST) to all protected areas and set up a broader network to improve the management of Asian elephant habitats in the cross boundary region between China and Laos. Specifically recipient will (1) strengthen professional capacity of staff in both China and Laos reserves to conduct survey and monitoring programs by implementing a standardized MIST protocol, (2) collect, analyze, and evaluate evidence of elephants, and assess the potential capacity in the region for elephant populations, (3) identify key priority corridors with GIS, GPS and Remote Sense technology for conservation action to immediately reduce poaching and to recover marginal agriculture land for habitat connectivity and elephants corridor restoration, and (4) develop the regional conservation action plan together with counterparts from both China and Laos.</narrative>
  </description>
